WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.822
Use this checkpoint to test conceptual understanding.

00:00:00.822 --> 00:00:01.622
Explain the row grain. Explain why an aggregate may be required.

00:00:01.622 --> 00:00:03.132
Explain the difference between missing and zero.

00:00:03.132 --> 00:00:03.502
Explain the common-type requirement for unpivoted values.

00:00:03.502 --> 00:00:03.842
And explain why an aggregate pivot-unpivot round trip cannot recreate original transactions.

00:00:03.842 --> 00:00:05.137
For this activity, make a prediction before you run anything.

00:00:05.137 --> 00:00:05.642
State what one output row should represent, which records you expect to remain,

00:00:05.642 --> 00:00:06.992
and what edge case is most likely to expose a mistake.

00:00:06.992 --> 00:00:07.582
Then run the SQL and compare the result with that prediction.

00:00:07.582 --> 00:00:08.032
If it does not match, debug the logic in small pieces instead of changing several clauses at once.

00:00:08.032 --> 00:00:08.332
This is the same habit you would use in a real analytics project:

00:00:08.332 --> 00:00:08.640
validate the meaning of the result, not only whether the statement executes.
